.TH CTI-APPSCAN 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-appscan \- weekly application-security report from the web-application scan notifications in the CTI mailbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-appscan
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-detail ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-text\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-auth\-fail\-out
.IR FILE ]
.PP
.B cti-appscan
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-detail ]
.B \-\-subject\-only
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-appscan
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-appscan
reads the Qualys WAS scan-completion notifications that arrived in the CTI
mailbox and builds the weekly AppSec report for the application-development
audience. It is normally run by
.BR run\-appscan (1)
from
.B cti\-agent\-appscan.timer
every Monday at 07:30, and the report is mailed by
.BR cti\-mailer (1)
.BR "\-\-lane was" ,
which resolves
.B WAS_TO
against
.B WAS_ALLOW_TO
and refuses if either is unset.
.PP
One run:
.TP
.B Reads the notifications
Every message in
.B GRAPH_FOLDER
of
.B GRAPH_MAILBOX
received within
.BR \-\-since .
Mail the fleet sent itself is skipped. Each message is offered to the known
scanners (Qualys WAS only, today); one that is recognised is parsed for the
scan's counts and authentication status. Notifications are deduplicated by
scan reference; one with no reference is kept and logged as not
deduplicated. Parse problems are logged as warnings.
.TP
.B Reconciles with the scan list
Unless
.B \-\-no\-detail
is given and when Qualys credentials are set, the WAS scan list for the
window is fetched and joined to the notifications. This supplies the real
application name and id, the portal link, and scans the scanner ran but
sent no email for (listed without counts). If the list cannot be read, the
report is built from the notifications alone and a warning says so.
.TP
.B Keeps the newest scan per application
Keyed by the scanner's application id, or by the whitespace-collapsed,
lower-cased name when there is no id.
.TP
.B Adds per-finding detail
Again unless
.BR \-\-no\-detail ,
the WAS Findings API is asked for the detail behind each notified scan's
counts. Any failure is a warning and costs only that application's detail.
.TP
.B Writes the report
HTML and plain text, both mode 0600: they say which applications have open
Urgent findings and which are scanned without authentication. Links point
only at known Qualys portal hosts; anything else is rendered as plain text.
.PP
A scan whose configured credential failed to authenticate is logged as
.B AUTH FAILED
and, with
.BR \-\-auth\-fail\-out ,
written to a file for
.B run\-appscan
to pass to
.BR cti\-alert (1).
That is the fleet operator's problem rather than the report audience's, and
this command does not send mail.
.PP
.B cti-appscan
sends nothing, changes nothing in the mailbox, and only reads from Qualys.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-out ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-since " DURATION"
How far back to read notifications, as a Go duration
.RB ( 168h ,
.BR 336h ).
Also the start of the scan-list and findings window. Not
.BR GRAPH_LOOKBACK_HOURS .
Default:\~\fB168h0m0s\fR (seven days).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-detail
Do not call the Qualys WAS API at all: no scan list, no findings. The
report carries the counts from the notifications only.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the HTML report to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-out " FILE"
Write the plain-text report to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600. If neither
.B \-\-out
nor
.B \-\-text\-out
is given, the text report goes to standard output.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.B \-\-subject\-only
Print the subject line on standard output and exit. The mailbox is read,
and the API called, exactly as for a full run; nothing is written, including
the
.B \-\-auth\-fail\-out
file.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-fail\-out " FILE"
Write one tab-separated line per scan whose configured credential failed:
application, authentication record, status. Mode 0600, and written on every
run, empty when nothing failed, so that an empty file ("checked, none
failed") can be told from an absent one ("not checked"). A failure to write
it is a warning, not a failed run.
Default:\~empty (not written).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.I fleet.env
is loaded at start from
.B FLEET_ENV
(else
.IR $FLEET_HOME/fleet.env ,
else
.IR /var/lib/cti\-agent/fleet.env );
variables already in the environment win.
.TP
.BR TENANT_ID ", " CLIENT_ID ", " CLIENT_SECRET ", " GRAPH_MAILBOX
Microsoft Graph, to read the mailbox. Required.
.I fleet.env
section 1.
.TP
.B GRAPH_FOLDER
Folder to read. Default:\~\fBinbox\fR. Section 1.
.TP
.BR QUALYS_BASE_URL ", " QUALYS_USERNAME ", " QUALYS_PASSWORD
The WAS API. Optional here: with
.B QUALYS_BASE_URL
or
.B QUALYS_USERNAME
empty the API is skipped, as with
.BR \-\-no\-detail ,
and a note says so. A
.B QUALYS_BASE_URL
that does not map to a known Qualys portal leaves report links as plain
text. Section 2.
.TP
.B FLEET_ORG
Organisation name in the report banner. Default:\~\fBSecurity\fR.
Section 4.
.TP
.BR GRAPH_LOOKBACK_HOURS ", " QUALYS_KB_MAX_AGE_HOURS ", " MAILBOX_LOOKBACK_HOURS ", " MAILBOX_MIN_AGE_HOURS
Not used, but validated by the shared configuration loader: a
non-integer value, or a mailbox window that breaks its rules (see
.BR cti\-agent (1)),
stops the run before anything is read.
.TP
.BR FLEET_ENV ", " FLEET_HOME
Locate
.IR fleet.env .
.PP
.BR WAS_TO " and " WAS_ALLOW_TO
are read by
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
not by this command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
Graph and Qualys credentials.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/appscan\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.{html,txt}
The report files written by
.BR run\-appscan ,
0600.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/appscan\-authfail\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.tsv
The authentication-failure file written for
.BR run\-appscan ,
0600. The runner deletes it before each run, so its absence afterwards
means the check did not happen.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report (or the subject) was produced. A scan list, findings lookup or
authentication-failure file that failed is a warning, not a failure;
authentication failures in the scans themselves do not change the exit
status either.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration missing or invalid (the message names the variables); the
mailbox could not be read; or a report file could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown option or an unparseable duration.
.B \-\-help
prints the usage and exits 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview the week's report without sending it:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-appscan \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
Counts only, from the notifications, printed to the terminal:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-appscan \-\-no\-detail
.EE
.PP
Two weeks instead of one:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-appscan \-\-since 336h \e
    \-\-text\-out /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/appscan\-two\-weeks.txt
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-appscan (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-alert (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 11f; fleet\-kit/README.md, "The weekly AppSec report".
